arm64e -> arm64 lowering for the iOS 27.2 userland (the Kryo 485 has no pointer authentication).

The scripts here are from UniXNU-zeta (https://github.com/none24smu/UniXNU-zeta, commit eb48928,
scripts/), BSD-2-Clause-Patent, see LICENSE.UniXNU-zeta. They prove every changed word is code
before lowering it (capstone 5 + llvm-mc) and redo the code-page hashes.

My change: rewrite-zeta-userland.py keeps each image's CodeDirectory flags and platform byte
(zeta adds CS_RUNTIME and platform 26 for macOS's AMFI; my kernel has its own AMFI).

Needs (WSL): python3 venv with capstone==5.0.3 and numpy, llvm-mc on PATH.
  root tree:   rewrite-zeta-userland-tree.py --root ROOT --output OUT --apple-trust-cache TC.im4p --report R.json
  dyld cache:  prove-zeta-dyld-cache.py, then rewrite-zeta-dyld-cache.py

Fast dyld cache pass (mine): fast-dyld-cache.py lowers every PAC word in the instruction sections without the
proof and writes the same work dir as prove-zeta-dyld-cache.py, then rewrite-zeta-dyld-cache.py applies it.
27.2 24B119: 34,315,608 edits (incl. 36 stub islands), 1 refused, 1.5 min.
